# Workspace -> output assignments.
#
# Keyed by stable output IDENTIFIER (make + model + serial), NOT connector
# name (DP-1/DP-2). The NVIDIA driver reshuffles which DisplayPort connector
# each physical monitor maps to across driver updates/reboots (observed
# 2026-05-28: DP-1 and DP-2 swapped monitors after an nvidia-driver update),
# so connector-based assignment lands workspaces on the wrong screen.
# Identifiers stay glued to the physical panel regardless of connector.
#
# Layout intent: ws 1-4 on the landscape monitor, ws 5-9 on the portrait one.
#   Landscape (right): LG Ultra HD, serial 0x00037F03
#   Portrait  (left):  LG HDR 4K,   serial 0x0007A9E5
#
# Use `number N` so we match the workspace number regardless of the dynamic
# name suffix added by autoname-workspaces.py.

workspace number 1 output "LG Electronics LG Ultra HD 0x00037F03"
workspace number 2 output "LG Electronics LG Ultra HD 0x00037F03"
workspace number 3 output "LG Electronics LG Ultra HD 0x00037F03"
workspace number 4 output "LG Electronics LG Ultra HD 0x00037F03"
workspace number 5 output "LG Electronics LG HDR 4K 0x0007A9E5"
workspace number 6 output "LG Electronics LG HDR 4K 0x0007A9E5"
workspace number 7 output "LG Electronics LG HDR 4K 0x0007A9E5"
workspace number 8 output "LG Electronics LG HDR 4K 0x0007A9E5"
